WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.500
For those looking to be thoroughly spooked,
Netflix is home to a wide array of unsettling

00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:08.620
horror movies, ranging anywhere from gory
slashers to tense psychological thrillers.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.620
To help you navigate the vast amount of Netflix
exclusives the platform has to offer, here's

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.980
a list of the creepiest Netflix films you
should never watch alone.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.820
After the unexpected death of their friend,
a group of old college buddies honor his memory

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.360
by taking a trip to Sweden.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.980
Shortly after embarking on their hiking journey,
one of the friends is injured, and the group

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.900
decides to take a shortcut through the forest.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.360
After a series of eerie occurrences, the group
becomes lost, turning what was supposed to

00:00:32.361 --> 00:00:36.730
be an adventurous trip commemorating their
lost pal into a disturbing, dangerous affair.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.480
The Ritual is at its strongest when it explores
the relationships and interactions between

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.380
the friends.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:45.620
As their sanity begins to slip, so does their
friendship, showing just how fragile the bond

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.840
between friends can be.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.700
The film offers a perfect blend of a good
story, creepy imagery, and a cast of likable

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.600
characters.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.420
The natural eeriness of the forest, the growing
tension as the group becomes more lost and

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:59.820
increasingly worse for wear, and the inclusion
of a sacrificial cult all make for a wonderfully

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.900
frightening flick.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:04.540
Just be careful about watching it before taking
any trips out to the forest.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.220
In Hush, Maddie Young is a deaf, mute author
who has moved into a remote house to write

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:10.240
her next book in peace.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.359
Unfortunately for the author, she gets trapped
in a twisted life or death scenario when a

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.900
stranger with a crossbow finds her isolated
home.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:21.079
Not only is Hush one of the best horror films
on Netflix, it's also one of the most suspenseful

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.060
films in the home invasion sub-genre.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:28.180
Director Mike Flannigan's expertise in tension-building
and creepy storytelling shine through effortlessly

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:30.780
in Hush, especially with the film's use of
sound.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.900
Because Maddie is deaf, Hush uses the natural
sound of a scene to help induce panic in the

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:35.760
audience.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.360
Viewers listening closely to the film will
be able to catch specific cues that escape

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.240
the main character.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.640
Before I Wake follows Jessie and her husband
Mark who take in a foster child named Cody

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.040
after their son passes away.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.460
Once Cody moves in, it becomes apparent to
the new parents that Cody is reluctant to

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.260
sleep.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:03.660
Turns out there's a good reason: Cody's dreams
become reality, which is especially awkward

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.429
as he keeps dreaming about their dead son.

00:02:05.429 --> 00:02:09.420
When Cody begins to dream of Jessie's deceased
child, the dynamic in the house immediately

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.260
changes.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:13.840
The parents struggle with accepting the passing
of the son when he keeps appearing in front

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:14.560
of them at night.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.700
But once Cody's dreams turn to nightmares,
the tone of the film changes from fantastical

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:19.780
to terrifying.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.860
In an attempt to rekindle their failing marriage,
Jessie and her husband Gerald take a vacation

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.800
to their lake house.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.680
Shortly after arriving, Gerald decides to
engage in some adventurous bedroom activity,

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.660
but he has a heart attack immediately after
he handcuffs Jessie, leaving her completely

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.540
trapped.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:38.519
Confined to her bed, Jessie must find a way
to escape while also facing off against a

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.740
starving dog and an ominous house guest that
visits her at night.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:48.260
"You're not real."

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.660
Gerald's Game is a brutal film to watch because
of the sheer helplessness of the protagonist

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:54.500
throughout the film.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.300
Her drive to stay alive and to free herself
creates a sense of optimism throughout the

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.300
film, but the obstacles in her way are absolutely
brutal.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:05.700
Wilfred James lives on a farm with his wife,
Arlette, and teenage son, Henry.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.860
Though Wilfred and Henry adore their simple
life, Arlette has other plans for the family.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:13.819
After she expresses her intent to sell the
farm and move to the city with Henry, tensions

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.240
quickly rise in the household.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:19.280
With limited options, Wilfred concludes that
to keep his land, he must kill his wife.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.300
1922 dives into the mind of a man willing
to kill for his own personal gain.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.960
The film frames the narrative through Wilfred's
telling of events.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:29.900
His inner monologues are eloquent and almost
poetic, but Wilfred is truly an unnerving

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.120
character to follow.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:40.480
"This is a thing I regret even more bitterly
than the crime for the reasons that this document

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.420
will show."

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.860
More terrifying than the killing itself is
how Wilfred's violent plot affects him and

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.360
the people he loves in ways he never believed
possible.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.439
The film doesn't shy away from showcasing
the consequences of Wilfred's depraved actions,

00:03:52.439 --> 00:03:56.750
and if you're looking for a slow-burn horror
film with a menacing main character, 1922

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.220
is definitely worth a watch.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:03.820
The Perfection focuses on Charlotte, a renowned
cellist who was forced to leave an elite conservatory.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.499
When Charlotte begins a relationship with
Elizabeth, the new prodigy from the same music

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.720
school, things quickly spiral out of control.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:14.460
The Perfection is genuinely unsettling, primarily
due to the strong acting of the two lead actresses.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.140
Both manage to be likable and unpredictable,
and it makes for a wild ride for viewers of

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.060
the film.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.180
With plenty of graphic imagery and disturbing
implications, The Perfection still manages

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.780
to be a thought-provoking watch.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:30.000
CAM follows Alice, a cam-girl who aspires
to rise to the top ranks of a cam-girl website.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.560
After she fakes killing herself on one of
her shows, Alice's account is hacked by a

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.700
person who looks and sounds identical to her.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.260
To get back her show and regain her identity,
Alice must find the source of the copycat

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:40.060
hacker.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:44.400
Not only is CAM a fun premise, the film smartly
comments on how women are treated in the adult

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.400
video industry.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.400
Alice is an extremely likable, confident woman
who is proud of her job as a cam-girl and

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.540
the audience she has acquired.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:54.419
The creepiness in CAM largely stems from how
easily someone's work and identity can be

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.420
stolen online.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:59.740
Alice's life is instantly destroyed, and there's
seemingly nothing she can do to protect herself.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:03.759
Considering just how easily accounts and even
major corporations can be hacked online, the

00:05:03.759 --> 00:05:07.340
implications in CAM should be more than enough
to make everybody delete their social media

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.580
accounts and permanently log off.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.060
Bird Box takes place in a frightening universe
where creatures drive anyone who looks at

00:05:14.069 --> 00:05:15.240
them to insanity.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:19.280
To avoid this fate, survivors must stay indoors
and cover their eyes when navigating outdoors.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:23.040
Malorie, an expectant mother, joins a group
of survivors in hopes of safely waiting out

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:23.900
the storm.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:28.060
With a child on the way and dwindling resources
among the group, Malorie must not only protect

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:31.800
herself but also find a way to safely raise
her newborn child in the post-apocalyptic

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:32.620
world.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.940
Bird Box presents a fascinating premise where
survivors must restrict the use of their eyes,

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.440
forcing them to find new ways to go on with
their daily lives.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.420
Most of the horror stems from having characters
walk around blindly, all while mentally unstable

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.680
people are trying to kill them.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:48.580
But the themes of motherhood and the fears
associated with it add an extra level of horror

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.080
that viewers are likely to find very unsettling.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:55.980
Serial killers are a staple of the horror
genre, but more often than not, we associate

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.720
them with monsters like Michael Myers and
Jason Voorhees rather than real life human

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.560
beings.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.960
But in Extremely Wicked, Shockingly Evil and
Vile, the focus isn't on some fictional slasher

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.270
but instead on Ted Bundy, the infamous serial
killer who murdered at least 30 women throughout

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.400
the 1970s.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:14.379
The film highlights Ted Bundy and his relationship
with his girlfriend, Liz Kendall, as they

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.620
weather the police's growing suspicions of
Bundy.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.540
Unknown to Liz, Ted is actively murdering
people while they're together and constantly

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:22.300
spinning lies to avoid detection.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:26.379
What makes Extremely Wicked, Shockingly Evil
and Vile an especially chilling watch isn't

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.580
gory killings or tense action set pieces.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.740
It's just how charismatic this killer is.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:35.160
Ted Bundy was an actual killer who killed
real people, often by manipulating his victims

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.260
into a false sense of security and preying
on their goodwill.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:43.720
"Whoever this woman is who's accusing you,
I'm sure she's just got you mixed up with

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:44.860
some other handsome stranger."

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:49.940
Set in the Australian Outback, Cargo follows
the trials and tribulations of Andy, a man

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:53.120
who's survived the zombie apocalypse, along
with his baby daughter Rosie.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:57.180
Unfortunately, Andy's recently been bitten,
and he only has a matter of hours before he

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.560
turns into one of the undead.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:03.280
With precious little time left, Andy's priority
is to find someone to raise his daughter after

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.980
he turns into one of the walking dead.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:09.240
Unlike many other zombie films, our hero Andy
is bitten early on, fated to die.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.360
As Andy's time diminishes and he becomes more
like the undead, we see not just the decline

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:15.800
of society but the fracturing of the family
unit.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:20.140
Cargo plays on the fear of complete isolation
and being mostly responsible for your own

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:23.120
survival, unable to seek out the help of others
in society.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:28.080
In Apostle, cultists living on a remote island
kidnap a woman and hold her for ransom.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.800
Sent on a mission to rescue his sister, Thomas
Richardson makes his way to the island to

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:32.600
save her.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:36.580
While covertly living among the cult members,
Thomas must navigate the island stealthily

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.400
and play the role of a devout follower.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:43.320
One of the bloodiest movies on Netflix, the
film features horrific rituals, creepy creatures,

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.580
and impressive action scenes.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:48.580
And when our hero discovers the full extent
of what's happening on this island, he realizes

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:51.389
he's caught up in something much darker than
he bargained for.

00:07:51.389 --> 00:07:55.009
As the film progresses, the beliefs of the
cult are slowly revealed, and the aggressive

00:07:55.009 --> 00:07:58.140
enforcement of those ideas helps to create
a sense of imminent dread for much of the

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:58.920
film.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:03.620
Apostle is the perfect creepy film for any
viewer that's at once terrified and fascinated

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:04.640
by cult life.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.180
I Am the Pretty Thing That Lives in the House
follows the story of Lily Saylor, a live-in

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:12.920
nurse who's hired to assist Iris Blum, a retired
writer with dementia.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:17.340
Once Lily begins to settle into the old house,
a series of strange events starts to occur,

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:20.740
like mold appearing on the walls and figures
of ghostly beings roaming the halls.

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:24.680
After finding a draft of one of Iris' books
detailing a murdered couple who once lived

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:28.460
in the house, Lily begins to suspect that
the account isn't fictional and that the home

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:29.320
might be haunted.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:33.060
For fans of paranormal thrillers, I Am the
Pretty Thing That Lives in the House makes

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:36.800
excellent use of the haunted mansion's creepy
atmosphere, with plenty of slow pans and dark

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:37.620
lighting.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:41.740
Instead of relying on jump scares and constant
threats, the film is more reserved, slowly

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.110
building up the paranormal happenings in Iris'
home.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:48.211
For viewers who may be tired of watching tweens
shrieking at CG ghosts and specters, the film

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:51.860
offers a refreshing change of pace that's
still likely to keep you awake at night.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:57.120
While serial killers, gory deaths, and dark
lighting all make for a creepy experience,

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.260
sometimes the scariest scenarios are a film's
psychological elements.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:04.660
In Clinical, Dr. Jane Mathis is a psychiatrist
struggling to move on with her life after

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.320
she's attacked by one of her patients.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.220
Relentlessly tortured by the idea that she
failed in her role as a psychiatrist, Jane

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:13.620
steps away from treating trauma patients to
focus on her own well-being.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:17.200
Just as she's beginning to make progress,
Jane receives a request from a man suffering

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:20.160
from trauma after an intense automobile accident.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.380
Moved by the man's plight, Vanessa agrees
to help him, but doing so has its consequences.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:28.060
Trying to juggle her mental health while also
fulfilling her promise to her new client begins

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:28.840
to take a toll.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:32.560
What separates this creepy Netflix horror
film from other movies is that it plays with

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.490
the concept of how scary a person's own mind
can be when they're not in control of it.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:41.290
Ghastly figures manifesting during sleep paralysis
and an unstable reality all come into play,

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:44.700
showing that sometimes the most severe and
dangerous struggles are constructed inside

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:45.860
our own minds.

